<title>UK: EU to approve Lagardere/Thompson deal - paper.</title>
<headline>EU to approve Lagardere/Thompson deal - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lagardere group's purchase of Thomson SA is expected to be cleared on Wednesday by Karel Van Miert, the European Union's competition commissioner, the Financial Times (FT) newspaper said.</p>
<p>Van Miert is also likely to give the all-clear to Daewoo Electronics to buy Thomson's consumer electronics division, Thomson Multimedia, the FT said.</p>
<p>However, Van Miert is expected to attach tough conditions to approve an 11 billion francs capital injection for Thomson from the French government to reduce part of its 25 billion franc debt, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>In October, the French government decided to sell Thomson for a symbolic one franc to Lagardere, whose interests span missiles firm Matra to book publisher Hachette.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
